Reported 2026-08-30 by Max from VS Code extension use (../lsp-openplanet-ext/).

## Symptom
Hovering a function/method in the editor does not show the arguments, and when
a name has more than one overload only one signature appears. Hover should show
as much detail as possible.

## Cause — verified by reading src/server/hover.rs on master @ 91a296c

Three separate defects, all in `src/server/hover.rs`:

### 1. Method hover prints a literally empty parameter list
`hover()` step 1 (the checked-view fast path, ~:56-58) does:

    } else if is_method_name(analysis, offset, &bare) {
        format!("(method) {} {}()", ty_display, bare)

`{}()` — the parens are hardcoded EMPTY. Any method hover renders
`(method) SomeType name()` with no arguments at all, ever.

Worse, this path RETURNS EARLY (~:64), so it shadows step 3
(`format_workspace_symbol`, ~:161) which does build a correct
`rt name(ty a, ty b)` signature. The good formatter is unreachable for
anything the checked view has a recorded type for.

### 2. External function hover drops every overload but the first
`lookup_external` (~:270):

    if let Some(fns) = index.lookup_function(qualified) {
        let func = &fns[0];

`lookup_function` returns a Vec precisely because AngelScript overloads. Hover
takes `[0]` and discards the rest, with no indication more exist. This is the
'no overloads' half of the report.

### 3. Workspace function hover is single-symbol by construction
`navigation::lookup_workspace_symbol` returns one `Symbol`, and
`format_workspace_symbol` formats that one. Overloaded workspace functions have
the same defect as (2).

## Also thin (same report, 'as much detail as possible')
- `lookup_external` type hover truncates properties and methods at
  `.take(6)` (~:246, :249) with NO '... N more' marker, so the user cannot tell
  the list is cut.
- Workspace symbols carry no doc comment in hover; only external functions do
  (`func.doc`, ~:288).
- No declaration location / source file shown for workspace symbols.
- Enum hover prints values but `format_workspace_symbol`'s Enum arm omits the
  values' numeric values, while `lookup_external`'s enum arm includes them —
  inconsistent between the two paths.

## Fix direction
- Give the checked-view method branch a real signature: resolve the method
  symbol and render its params, or fall through to the workspace/external
  formatter instead of returning early with `()`.
- Render the FULL overload set for both external and workspace functions: one
  code-fenced signature per overload, in a stable (deterministic) order.
- Replace the bare `.take(6)` truncation with a marker naming the remaining
  count, or raise/remove the cap.
- Unify the two formatters so external and workspace symbols present the same
  fields (signature, doc, enum values) rather than diverging.

## Test plan (TDD, red first)
Existing hover tests live in `src/server/hover.rs` `mod tests` (~:317+) and use
`pos_of` + a fixture source — follow that pattern.

Red:
- `hover_method_shows_parameters`: hover a method call with 2 params -> the
  rendered hover CONTAINS the parameter types and names (fails today: `()`).
- `hover_shows_all_overloads`: a function with 3 overloads -> all 3 signatures
  present (fails today: 1).
- `hover_external_overloads_listed`: same against a typedb function with
  multiple entries in the `lookup_function` Vec.

Variants (per CLAUDE.md, generalize):
- overload counts 1 / 2 / 5 — a single overload must NOT gain list formatting
  or a '1 overload' header
- overload ordering is deterministic across runs (guard against HashMap order)
- param modifiers render: `const T &in`, `T &out`, `T &inout`, `T@`,
  `T@ &in`, `const T@`, plain `T`, and a defaulted param `int x = 3`
- zero-param function -> `()` is CORRECT here; assert no stray comma
- variadic / unnamed params (typedb `name: None` -> `_`) still render
- methods vs free functions vs namespaced functions vs funcdefs
- a method on a class with a base class (inherited method hover)
- workspace symbol AND external symbol paths both covered for each of the above
- type hover with >6 properties/methods shows a remaining-count marker
- enum hover shows values consistently on both the workspace and external paths

## Related
Extension repo: ../lsp-openplanet-ext/ (packages/vscode-ext). No extension-side
change is expected — this is server-side hover content — but confirm the
extension does not post-process or truncate hover markdown before rendering.